<title>KENYA: SOCCER-AFRICAN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of African group World</p>
<p>Cup soccer qualifiers on Sunday:</p>
<p>Group one</p>
<p>In Nairobi): Kenya beat Guinea 1-0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Musa Otieno (3, pen)</p>
<p>Attendance: 55,000</p>
<p>Group three</p>
<p>In Lusaka: Zambia beat Congo 3-0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Dennis Lota (40), Johnston Bwalya (88), Mwape Miti</p>
<p>(89)</p>
<p>Group four</p>
<p>In Harrare: Zimbabwe and Angola drew 0-0</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>In Douala: Cameroon beat Togo 2-0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Bernard Tchoutang (85) Patrick Mboma (88)</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p>In Tunis: Tunisia beat Liberia 2-0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Adel Sellimi 60 pen, Khaled Badra 78</p>
<p>Attendance: 38,000</p>
<p>Group Five</p>
<p>In Accra: Ghana beat Gabon 3-0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Felix Aboagye 42, Mohamed Gargo 60, 63 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p>In Ouagadougou: Nigeria beat Burkina Faso 2-1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Nigeria - Mangaoule Diabate 40 own goal, Emmanuel Amunike 58</p>
<p>Burkina - Mamadou Zongo 76</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>In Lome:</p>
<p>Group three</p>
<p>Zaire 1 South Africa 2 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Zaire - Zico Tumba (25)</p>
<p>South Africa - Doctor Khumalo (21), Phil Masinga (71)</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,000</p>
<p>    Standings    P  W  D  L  F  A PTS</p>
<p>    Congo	  4  2  1  1  4  4  7</p>
<p>South Africa 4  2  1  1  3  3  7</p>
<p>    Zambia	 4  1  2  1  5  3  5</p>
<p>    Zaire	  4  0  2  2  5  7  2</p>
<p>Next matches: Congo v Zaire, Pointe Noire, June 8,</p>
<p>South Africa v Zambia, Johannesburg, June 8</p>
</text>
